{"Buj": [{"id": "Buj", "headword": "भुज्", "headword_slp1": "Buj", "fold": "Buj", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "1 भुज् भुज॑ति pp. भुग्न (q.v.) bend, turn, make\ncrooked. — अव & आ bend in. नि bend down. निस् & विनिस् bend\naside, turn away. परि encompass, embrace. प्र bend, fold. — Cf.\nआभुग्न, व्याभुग्न.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "2 भुज् भुन॑क्ति भुङ्क्ते॑ (भुञ्जति, ˚ते), pp.\nभुक्त (q.v.) enjoy (in older lang. w. instr., later mostly w. acc.),\nesp. food (i.e. eat, feed on, ± acc.), but also the earth, a country or\ntown (i.e. rule), a woman (i.e. love carnally), etc.;\n experience,\nendure, atone for (acc.) at the hands of (gen.);\n be of use to, serve\n(acc.). C. भोजयति (˚ते) cause to enjoy or eat, feed (acc. of\npers. & acc. or instr. of th.). D. बुभुक्षते (˚ति) wish to eat, be\nhungry. I. बोभुजीति enjoy. — अनु reap the fruit of (acc.), partake\nof, enjoy. अभि be of service to (acc.). उप enjoy (also carnally),\neat, consume, use, possess, partake of, live on, reap the fruit of\n(acc.);\n be of use or service to (acc.). परि eat before another or\nleave another without food (acc.);\n eat, devour, use, employ. सम् eat\ntogether, keep a common meal, enjoy (also carnally). C. cause to eat,\nfeed with (instr.).", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "3 भु॑ज् f. enjoyment, profit, advantage, service, use,\npossession, wealth (dat. भुजे॑ also as infin.);\n adj. —˚ enjoying,\neating, ruling, loving etc. (v. prec.)", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "Buja": [{"id": "Buja", "headword": "भुज", "headword_slp1": "Buja", "fold": "Buja", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "भुज m. arm, branch, trunk of an elephant;\n f. आ the coil\nof a snake, arm.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["भुजः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["BujaH"]}], "Bujaga": [{"id": "Bujaga", "headword": "भुजग", "headword_slp1": "Bujaga", "fold": "Bujaga", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sa